  "_comment": "Term list for the course. NOTHING IN THIS FILE BLOCKS ANYTHING, and nothing in it is a budget. The vocabulary ratchet that enforced per-term unlock units was retired 2026-09-03 on JM's call. The 47-unit sequence those unlock ids were keyed to was struck from `structurephilosophy.md` on 2026-09-17, along with the course-length, term-budget, naming-delay and per-arc minute budgets that used to sit in this file; they are gone rather than stale. The live rule is simpler and stricter: no vocabulary is taught in the lessons at all, jargon is avoided in student-facing prose, and the only terms that may appear are biological ones an introductory student already has (meiosis, allele, gene, locus). Technical names are still legal inside the R code panel. What reads this file is `check_lessons.py --terms`, which reports where each term is first named in the shipped lessons, in lesson-number order; `giveaway_phrases` and `stage0_mechanism_lexicon` feed `--style`. Both are advisory reports for whoever is drafting.",
